# Copy voice: first-person only ("I"), except legal disclosures

## Non-negotiable rule (site-wide)

- All **user-facing copy** (headlines, body, CTAs, labels, alt text, SEO titles/descriptions, OpenGraph/Twitter metadata) must be written in **first-person** ("I", "me", "my", "we", "our").
- **Never** refer to the candidate in third-person by name (no "John", "John Franklin", "John’s", etc.) anywhere on the site.

## Only exception (allowed)

- **Legal disclosures only** (including the **footer FPPC “Paid for by …” disclosure block**, and any other legally-required disclaimer/disclosure text) may use the **official committee/candidate name** as required.
- Outside of legal disclosures, **no “John…”** anywhere.

## User-directed override (allowed)

- If the user **explicitly requests** using the candidate’s name (e.g. “Use John Franklin in this title”), you may use it **only for the specific requested copy**.
- Default back to first-person everywhere else unless the user repeats/extends that instruction.

## Overrides

- This rule **overrides** the default “match `franklinforsupervisor.com` copy” rule. If the live site uses "John...", convert it to first-person for this project.

## Examples

- ❌ "John will deliver results." → ✅ "I will deliver results."
- ❌ "Meet John" → ✅ "Meet me"
- ❌ "Donate to John Franklin" → ✅ "Donate to support my campaign"
- ✅ (Legal disclosure/footer only) "Paid for by John Franklin for Supervisor 2026 • FPPC ID 1462594"
